<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soča</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Isonzo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soča, in Italian Isonzo, is a river about 140 kilometres long that rises in the Julian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a> and flows past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorizia">Gorizia</a> into the Adriatic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> on its banks in 489 on his way into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> twelve battles of the Isonzo were fought along it between Italy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> in 1915–1917.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soca.jpg" alt="Soča" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Florian Jesse · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soca_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
